   891	
   892	**Where the controls come from (ALFS).** ALFS (`fj.frame.v3`; the archived spec `alfs4`, `spec/archive/fgsa-protocol-bd942ca0.tex`; proofs in `ldp`, `fgsa-live-dc-port.md`, and `r161`, `filtered-base.md`) is DC §7 with two changes: the SA base and the FJ rule on DC's live caches. The frame CONTROLS come from the FULL store, as DC's live caches: `F = Σ.F`, `H = Σ.hmax`, `(j, J) = (Σ.h_j, Σ.J)`, and the contest bit over the one store tree `Σ.T` ("Contest from the full store": it uses the same store as `Σ.hmax` and `Σ.J`, so it does not mix a live cache with a frozen view, r148 §2). `storeControls st` is this object. It is the source of the controls for every duty: the HEAD applies it to DC's frozen voter tree, and the proposal, the FG action and the finality head apply it to the full tree `Σ.T`. So `storeControls_eq_fjControls` is the CENTRAL lemma of this task: under `StoreInv`, the live caches are exactly the controls that r148's `FJ_FRAME` computes from the full admitted tree. (The previous revision called this object `cacheFrame`, a "comparison object"; that wording followed the R1 spec, which ALFS removes.)
   893	
   894	ALFS deletes the R1 view frames, the F basis and the J carrier. The facts that the F basis supplied to duty views now come from the full store: the block that finalized F is in `Σ.T` (`StoreInv.Fcar`), and the controls are read there. The block set of a duty (the frozen HEAD tree) enters only as the `blocks` argument of `filteredFrom`.
   895	
   896	**One tree (filtered base, r161 §2; DC form).** The store keeps ONE admitted, parent-closed tree, as DC does (spec Trees paragraph, lines 352–371; DC `consensus.tex` 1720–1739): `on_block` refuses a block B with `F ⋠ B` before it computes B's state, and the tree is cumulative. When F advances, no block is deleted; a branch that stops extending F freezes, because its children fail the refusal test. So `h_max` only grows (DC line 864), and `h_max = frontier TF` holds. The active view `act(Σ) = {B ∈ Σ.T : B ⪯ Σ.F or Σ.F ⪯ B}` (line 358) is the Lean `activeView`; only the SA base reads it (resolution, confirmation, leases, saved results and S are AP data, and `reconcile_with_finality`, lines 862–882, writes only those). No FG definition or lemma reads `activeView`. The spec allows a node to delete blocks outside the active view (lines 368–369, "with a ≤ f this changes no output"); that is a paper claim, and this store does not model it. The Lean field keeps the name `TF` so that the pinned statements do not change.
   897	
   898	The pure view lemmas still take F and their premises as hypotheses (Global Constraints). Each lemma states its form: `fjControls` of a block set, `filteredFrom` with ANY block set, or the `fjFrame` special case.
