   903	/-- The FG part of a node store (DC-fj). `TF` is the ONE admitted,
   904	parent-closed tree (the spec's `Σ.T`, Trees paragraph, alfs4 lines 352–371;
   905	initialization 474–482; DC `consensus.tex` 1720–1739). The spec admits a block
   906	B only if `F ⪯ B` at that time (line 354); this history is NOT formalized (no
   907	ghost field records it), and no lemma needs it. The tree is cumulative: no block is
   908	deleted when F advances. There is no raw tree. `F`, `J`, `h_j` and `h_max` are
   909	DC's live caches; they are the frame controls. `h_max` only grows (DC line
   910	864). The field keeps the name `TF` so that the pinned statements do not
   911	change. -/
   912	structure Store (V : Type) where
   913	  TF : Finset (FGBlock V)
   914	  F : FGBlock V
   915	  J : FGBlock V
   916	  h_j : Height
   917	  h_max : Height
   918	
   919	def Store.init : Store V := ⟨{.genesis}, .genesis, .genesis, 0, 1⟩
   920	
