  1180	    - `gen`: the tree only grows.
  1181	    - `Fmem`: F moves only to `σ.F ∈ acceptViable ⊆ TF`.
  1182	    - `hmax`: `frontier (insert B TF) = max (frontier TF) (h B)`, and `update_finality` sets `h_max := max h_max (h B)`. No block leaves the tree, so `h_max` stays the frontier (DC line 864). A refused block changes nothing (G04).
  1183	    - `pair`: a new pair enters only if `F ⪯ σ.J` and it is lex-greater; otherwise the old pair stays the lex-max over the larger tree. When F advances to `σ.F ⪯ J`, the cached pair still has `F ⪯ J`. Every other pair with `new F ⪯ J'` also had `old F ⪯ J'`, because `old F ⪯ new F`. So the lex-max does not change. A stored block that conflicts with the new F has no pair with `new F ⪯ J'`, so it cannot be selected. `hinj` makes the selected pair unique.
