   745	**Controls and the filtered tree (ALFS).** ALFS is the DC form of FG-SA, registered as `fj.frame.v3` (registry commit `648f255`; source key `alfs4`, the archived spec `spec/archive/fgsa-protocol-bd942ca0.tex`; proof files `ldp`, `fgsa-live-dc-port.md`, and `r161`, `filtered-base.md`). In ALFS the frame has two parts:
   746	- the CONTROLS `(F, H, j, J, contest)`, with the derived root `Z` and band floor `lo` (`fg_contest`, `band_floor` and `get_fg_root`, `alfs4` lines 970–986 and 1004–1011). ALFS reads them from the FULL store, as DC's live caches: `F = Σ.F`, `H = Σ.hmax`, `(j, J) = (Σ.h_j, Σ.J)`, and the contest over the one store tree `Σ.T`. Task 7's `storeControls` is this form, and `storeControls_eq_fjControls` shows that it equals `fjControls Σ.F Σ.T` under the store invariant;
   747	- the FILTERED TREE `filteredFrom c blocks` over an explicit block set: `get_filtered_block_tree_from(Σ, blocks)` (`alfs4` lines 1013–1020), that is `viable_tree_from(Σ, blocks)` (lines 988–994) cut at the root, `{B ∈ blocks : F ⪯ B, Z ⪯ B, ∃ W ∈ blocks, B ⪯ W, h(W) ≥ lo}`. The HEAD walks it over DC's frozen voter tree (`voter_processed_block_tree` and `voter_filtered_block_tree`, lines 1207–1222; the HEAD duty call, lines 1283–1285) with the full-store controls; the proposal, the FG action and the finality head use the full tree `Σ.T` (`get_filtered_block_tree`, lines 1021–1025). The block sets, the walk start `live_root` (lines 1074–1086: the deepest live lease in the full filtered tree, else the FG root) and `get_head_in_tree` (lines 1088–1095) are AP data.
