   778	  This checks that the contest changes both viability and `lo`. It does not test eligibility: eligibility is the AP's.
   779	
   780	- [ ] **Step 2: Write `Frame.lean`.**
   781	
   782	```lean
   783	abbrev View (V : Type) := Finset (FGBlock V)
   784	
   785	variable {V : Type} [DecidableEq V] [Fintype V] (E : Electorate V) (cfg : FGConfig)
   786	
   787	def hOf (W : FGBlock V) : Height := (derive E cfg W).h
   788	
   789	/-- `H = max({1} ∪ {h(W) : W ∈ V})`. -/
   790	def frontier (Vw : View V) : Height := Vw.sup (hOf E cfg) ⊔ 1
   791	
   792	/-- Collision freedom on a view: roots identify the blocks of the view and their
   793	ancestors (the collision-free hash idealization; DC `RootInjectiveOnAncestors`).
   794	A hypothesis of every lemma that reads the selected pair; no definition assumes
   795	it. -/
   796	def ViewRootInj (Vw : View V) : Prop :=
   797	  ∀ X Y, (∃ W ∈ Vw, FGBlock.Preceq X W) → (∃ W ∈ Vw, FGBlock.Preceq Y W) →
   798	    X.root = Y.root → X = Y
   799	
   800	/-- The lex key `(h_j, J.root)`. -/
   801	def lexKey (p : Height × FGBlock V) : Lex (ℕ × ℕ) := toLex (p.1, p.2.root.value)
   802	
   803	/-- The frame controls (ALFS: DC's live caches). The root and the band floor
   804	are functions of them (r148 FJ_FRAME table). -/
   805	structure Controls (V : Type) where
   806	  F : FGBlock V
   807	  H : Height
   808	  j : Height
   809	  J : FGBlock V
   810	  contest : Bool
   811	
   812	namespace Controls
   813	/-- The uncontested phase: the root is J. -/
   814	def rootIsJ (c : Controls V) : Bool := decide (c.H = c.j + 1) && !c.contest
   815	def Z (c : Controls V) : FGBlock V := if c.rootIsJ then c.J else c.F
   816	def lo (c : Controls V) : Height := if c.contest then c.H else c.H - 1
   817	end Controls
   818	
   819	structure Frame (V : Type) where
   820	  F : FGBlock V
   821	  H : Height
   822	  j : Height
   823	  J : FGBlock V
   824	  Z : FGBlock V
   825	  lo : Height
   826	  D : Finset (FGBlock V)
   827	  contest : Bool
   828	```
   829	
   830	  `lexMax E cfg F Vw` returns the lex-greatest `(h_j, J)` over `W ∈ Vw` with `F ⪯ (derive W).J`, or `(0, genesis)` if there is none:
   831	  - Compute the greatest key with `Finset.sup` over `Lex (ℕ × ℕ)`.
   832	  - Take the pair with that key through `pickPair`, a port of DC's `pickUnique?` (`DC/DecoupledConsensusModel/Objects/Blocks.lean:295–301`), on the Finset of candidate PAIRS (the image of the view, so that two carriers of one pair count once), with `(0, genesis)` as the default.
   833	  - `pickPair` has DC's tie behavior: it returns the unique candidate with the greatest key, and `none` when two DISTINCT candidates have that key (a root collision). Then `lexMax` falls back to `(0, genesis)`. Do not choose one of them: there is no computable order on `FGBlock` that the spec names.
   834	  - Under `ViewRootInj Vw`, two candidates with one key are one pair (same `h_j`, same root, so the same J), so `pickPair` returns it. Every lemma that reads the selected pair (`lexMax_of_candidate`, `lexMax_mono`, `fjFrame_D_nonempty`, the Task 12 and 13 lemmas) has `ViewRootInj` as a hypothesis. `storeControls_eq_fjControls` (Task 7) takes `StoreInv` only: `StoreInv.pair` already equates the cache with the selected pair, and `ViewRootInj` is used only by `storeInv_on_block`, to keep `pair`.
   835	  - Keep `lexMax` computable, so that the `decide` examples reduce.
   836	
   837	  The fallback `(0, genesis)`: if `F ≠ genesis` and no pair in the view extends F, then `J = genesis`, and `F ⪯ J` fails. In ALFS the controls come from the full store, which holds the block that finalized F (`StoreInv.Fcar`, Task 7), so the fallback is not used there. Task 7's `lexMax_of_candidate` (a helper) proves that the fallback is not used when the block set holds a block whose J extends F and `ViewRootInj` holds. Keep the fallback; do not change it to `(h_F, F)`, because the spec does not say so.
   838	
   839	
   840	  Write `fjFrame` through the two parts, and keep its fields:
   841	
   842	```lean
   843	/-- [pin fj.frame.v1] The controls of one block set (r148 §2 FJ_FRAME, R1 view
   844	form): H, the lex pair with `F ⪯ J`, and the contest at `H = j+1` when a
   845	height-H block does not extend J. -/
   846	def fjControls (F : FGBlock V) (Vw : View V) : Controls V :=
   847	  let H := frontier E cfg Vw
   848	  let p := lexMax E cfg F Vw
   849	  ⟨F, H, p.1, p.2, decide (H = p.1 + 1) &&
   850	    decide (∃ W ∈ Vw, hOf E cfg W = H ∧ ¬ FGBlock.Preceq p.2 W)⟩
   851	
   852	/-- [pin fj.frame.v3] The filtered tree of any block set under given controls
   853	(`get_filtered_block_tree_from(Σ, blocks)` with `viable_tree_from`, alfs4 lines
   854	988–994, 1013–1020). -/
   855	def filteredFrom (c : Controls V) (blocks : Finset (FGBlock V)) : Finset (FGBlock V) :=
   856	  blocks.filter (fun B => FGBlock.preceq c.F B && FGBlock.preceq c.Z B &&
   857	    decide (∃ W ∈ blocks, FGBlock.Preceq B W ∧ c.lo ≤ hOf E cfg W))
   858	
   859	/-- [pin fj.frame.v1] The special case: controls and filtered tree from one
   860	block set. -/
   861	def fjFrame (F : FGBlock V) (Vw : View V) : Frame V :=
   862	  let c := fjControls E cfg F Vw
   863	  ⟨c.F, c.H, c.j, c.J, c.Z, c.lo, filteredFrom E cfg c Vw, c.contest⟩
   864	```
